      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "HELLO WORLD\n\nThe smallest useful Blueprint. A class is a graph of nodes joined by wires:\n  white wires carry EXECUTION (what runs next), coloured wires carry DATA (values).\nWhen the game starts, the Begin Play event fires and the white wire runs the\nnodes to its right, left to right. Compile with F7, then press Play and look at the log.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. EVENT\nBegin Play is an entry point: it has no input exec pin, only an output (Body). It runs once when the object enters the game.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -50.0
        ],
        "size": [
          270.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. PRINT\nPrint String (println) writes its Message input to the console. The Message pin has no wire, so the text you type on the node is the value.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          -50.0
        ],
        "size": [
          270.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "say"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. LOG\nlog_info writes to the engine log (with a level and source), so it can be filtered; plain prints go to the console only.",
        "position": [
          660.0,
          -50.0
        ],
        "size": [
          270.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
